1048
00:45:59,267 --> 00:46:00,567
- [Tom] It's like a pork hock.

1049
00:46:00,567 --> 00:46:02,133
- Jan in the Pan,
are you still here?

1050
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:05,600
- [Tom] Aw, doggone it.

1051
00:46:05,600 --> 00:46:07,833
I always set down my
coffee and then lose it.

1052
00:46:09,467 --> 00:46:10,467
It's the rabbit mug.

1053
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:13,400
- And I'm not the first.

1054
00:46:15,233 --> 00:46:18,033
Knock twice if
I'm not the first.

1055
00:46:18,033 --> 00:46:20,733
(knocking twice)

1056
00:46:20,733 --> 00:46:22,233
- [Mike] Oh, this is hot. Hot.

1057
00:46:26,933 --> 00:46:28,567
- He should've let me die.

1058
00:46:28,567 --> 00:46:30,533
- Oh, are you still on that?

1059
00:46:30,533 --> 00:46:32,267
Well, we've got
problems too, lady.

1060
00:46:32,267 --> 00:46:33,900
- I hate him for
what he's done to me.

1061
00:46:33,900 --> 00:46:34,800
- [Mike] Which is?

1062
00:46:36,900 --> 00:46:39,500
- If he only knew what
it's like being like this.

1063
00:46:39,500 --> 00:46:40,433
- [Tom] Oh, as if
you're the only one

1064
00:46:40,433 --> 00:46:41,900
who ever got their head cut off.

1065
00:46:41,900 --> 00:46:42,933
Quit whining!

1066
00:46:43,967 --> 00:46:46,367
- Do you know what it's like?

1067
00:46:47,600 --> 00:46:49,033
(something knocking)

1068
00:46:49,033 --> 00:46:51,867
- [Mike] Hey, it's
lights out down there.

1069
00:46:51,867 --> 00:46:53,100
Geez.

1070
00:46:53,100 --> 00:46:54,733
- Together we
could have revenge.

1071
00:46:54,733 --> 00:46:57,933
- Revenge, a dish
best served, oh.

1072
00:46:57,933 --> 00:46:59,400
- Want revenge?

1073
00:46:59,400 --> 00:47:01,800
- [Tom] No, I want to
sleep. Would you shut up?

1074
00:47:01,800 --> 00:47:04,867
(something knocking)

1075
00:47:08,833 --> 00:47:10,433
- [Mike] I want to join
in their conversation,

1076
00:47:10,433 --> 00:47:12,000
but I don't know what to say.

1077
00:47:14,400 --> 00:47:16,433
- I wonder if "Silk
Stalkings" is on yet?

1078
00:47:19,533 --> 00:47:21,733
- Yes.

1079
00:47:21,733 --> 00:47:24,567
You the thing inside, and
me the thing out here.

1080
00:47:24,567 --> 00:47:26,933
- [Tom] I'm just
freeforming here.

1081
00:47:26,933 --> 00:47:28,900
- My brain's still untouched.

1082
00:47:30,100 --> 00:47:31,633
And his keeping me
alive has given me

1083
00:47:31,633 --> 00:47:33,233
a power he didn't count on.

1084
00:47:33,233 --> 00:47:35,133
- [Mike] The power
of Matthew Star.

1085
00:47:36,433 --> 00:47:37,833
- A power that you can feel,

1086
00:47:39,467 --> 00:47:41,533
across this room and
through that door.

1087
00:47:41,533 --> 00:47:43,867
♪ To grandmother's house we go ♪

1088
00:47:43,867 --> 00:47:45,500
- Can't you?

1089
00:47:45,500 --> 00:47:48,600
(something knocking)

1090
00:47:50,600 --> 00:47:51,633
- [Tom] Oh, I'll
tell them a joke

1091
00:47:51,633 --> 00:47:53,900
I heard on "Arsenio" last night.

1092
00:47:53,900 --> 00:47:55,900
- [Mike] Ooh, I sat
on someone's hand.

1093
00:47:55,900 --> 00:47:58,467
He leaves his experiments
lying all over the house.

1094
00:48:02,000 --> 00:48:03,167
- Get me the president.

1095
00:48:07,033 --> 00:48:09,033
- Together, we're
both more than things.

1096
00:48:10,567 --> 00:48:13,033
We have a power as hideous
as our deformities.

1097
00:48:13,033 --> 00:48:14,867
- [Tom] Speak for yourself!

1098
00:48:14,867 --> 00:48:15,967
- Together, we'll
wreak our revenge.

1099
00:48:15,967 --> 00:48:17,800
- [Mike] Well, you already reek.

1100
00:48:19,133 --> 00:48:22,600
- I shall create power.

1101
00:48:22,600 --> 00:48:24,367
And you will enforce it.

1102
00:48:24,367 --> 00:48:25,200
- That's nice, honey.

1103
00:48:25,200 --> 00:48:26,433
Look, I'm gonna turn in.

1104
00:48:26,433 --> 00:48:31,200
- You the thing inside,
me the thing out here.

1105
00:48:31,933 --> 00:48:33,433
- [Tom] Great.

1106
00:48:33,433 --> 00:48:34,433
You know, you should come
to our Tuesday night group.

1107
00:48:35,567 --> 00:48:36,800
- [Mike] I've got it.

1108
00:48:36,800 --> 00:48:38,200
If I wander around
here some more,

1109
00:48:38,200 --> 00:48:39,833
it'll keep the budget down.

1110
00:48:39,833 --> 00:48:42,000
- [Tom] Yes, yes.

1111
00:48:42,000 --> 00:48:45,100
- I'm going to make a decision.

1112
00:48:45,100 --> 00:48:46,367
No, no.

1113
00:48:46,367 --> 00:48:48,467
- [Tom] Bill Clinton
in the Oval Office.

1114
00:48:48,467 --> 00:48:49,300
- That's it!

1115
00:48:50,433 --> 00:48:51,267
No it isn't.

1116
00:48:52,967 --> 00:48:53,800
Yes! No.

1117
00:48:55,800 --> 00:48:56,733
- [Mike] Yes. No?

1118
00:48:57,667 --> 00:48:58,700
Maybe. Yes.

1119
00:48:58,700 --> 00:49:00,067
No.

1120
00:49:00,067 --> 00:49:00,867
- Yes.

1121
00:49:04,467 --> 00:49:05,600
- [Tom] Hi, you decent?

1122
00:49:08,200 --> 00:49:11,200
(suspenseful music)

1123
00:49:15,800 --> 00:49:17,233
- [Mike] I'm in the tub.

1124
00:49:17,233 --> 00:49:19,100
- She's always in the tub.

1125
00:49:19,100 --> 00:49:20,633
- [Mike] Oh.

1126
00:49:20,633 --> 00:49:21,733
- Mrs. Carmichael?

1127
00:49:26,267 --> 00:49:27,400
- [Tom] I was gonna
make some popcorn.

1128
00:49:27,400 --> 00:49:29,033
Do you want, uh, oh yeah.

1129
00:49:31,067 --> 00:49:32,500
- [Mike] Anybody seen my wallet?

1130
00:49:32,500 --> 00:49:34,367
Oh, don't get up. I'll find it.

1131
00:49:35,800 --> 00:49:37,033
- Don't mind me.

1132
00:49:37,033 --> 00:49:38,800
Just keep doing whatever
it was you were doing.

1133
00:49:43,567 --> 00:49:46,200
- Maybe she could get work
in a Peter Gabriel video.

1134
00:49:46,200 --> 00:49:47,033
- [Tom] Cool.

1135
00:49:49,833 --> 00:49:53,400
- [Mike] Hello,
Mr. Thing? Hello?

1136
00:49:59,033 --> 00:50:00,600
- [Tom] Doh!

1137
00:50:00,600 --> 00:50:02,200
(Jan laughing)

1138
00:50:02,200 --> 00:50:05,200
- If I had sides, they'd
be splitting right now.

1139
00:50:07,167 --> 00:50:09,467
I'm sorry. It was
just really funny.

1140
00:50:11,733 --> 00:50:13,633
- [Tom] Getting
her juice up there.

1141
00:50:13,633 --> 00:50:15,533
- [Mike] Ew, she's
getting cradle cap.

1142
00:50:18,367 --> 00:50:20,933
- What's locked
behind that door?

1143
00:50:20,933 --> 00:50:24,333
- [Tom] I don't know, what's
locked behind that door?

1144
00:50:24,333 --> 00:50:26,600
- No normal mind could imagine.

1145
00:50:26,600 --> 00:50:28,900
Something even more
terrible than you.

1146
00:50:28,900 --> 00:50:29,867
- Oh, and our bicycles.

1147
00:50:29,867 --> 00:50:33,200
- No, my deformed friend.

1148
00:50:33,200 --> 00:50:38,133
Like all quantities, horror
has its ultimate, and I'm that.

1149
00:50:40,367 --> 00:50:42,767
- There is a horror
beyond yours.

1150
00:50:42,767 --> 00:50:44,133
And it's in there.

1151
00:50:44,133 --> 00:50:45,100
- [Mike] It's Pauly Shore.
(Tom gasping)

1152
00:50:45,100 --> 00:50:46,400
- Locked behind that door.

1153
00:50:46,400 --> 00:50:48,200
- Beside which Carol
Merrill is standing.

1154
00:50:49,500 --> 00:50:51,633
- Miles of experimentation
twist and turn

1155
00:50:51,633 --> 00:50:53,333
through mountains
of miscalculation

1156
00:50:53,333 --> 00:50:56,733
and often lose themselves
in error and darkness.

1157
00:50:56,733 --> 00:50:58,200
- [Mike] And sometimes
things just screw up.

1158
00:50:58,200 --> 00:51:01,233
- Behind that door
is the sum total

1159
00:51:01,233 --> 00:51:02,700
of Dr. Cortner's mistakes.

1160
00:51:02,700 --> 00:51:03,967
- A guy named Murray.

1161
00:51:05,100 --> 00:51:07,367
- [Tom] Well, I gotta
roll. I'll see ya.

1162
00:51:07,367 --> 00:51:09,967
- He had no right to
bring me back to this.

1163
00:51:11,133 --> 00:51:13,467
- [Tom] Boy, you have a
chip on your shoulder.

1164
00:51:13,467 --> 00:51:14,733
Ooh, did it again.

1165
00:51:14,733 --> 00:51:15,567
- Who knows?

1166
00:51:16,467 --> 00:51:17,767
But you should know.

1167
00:51:17,767 --> 00:51:19,733
- This operation's gonna
cost an arm and a leg.

1168
00:51:19,733 --> 00:51:20,933
- [Tom] Zing! Ooh!

1169
00:51:20,933 --> 00:51:22,600
- The doctor injected
a serum into that.

1170
00:51:22,600 --> 00:51:25,133
It was but a mass
of grafted tissues.

1171
00:51:25,133 --> 00:51:26,333
Lifeless.

1172
00:51:27,767 --> 00:51:30,200
It just lay there, weighted
down with its transplants

1173
00:51:30,200 --> 00:51:32,333
of broken limbs
and amputated arms.

1174
00:51:33,433 --> 00:51:36,167
But with this serum-
- I thee wed.

1175
00:51:36,167 --> 00:51:37,967
- It, it began to breathe.

1176
00:51:37,967 --> 00:51:39,167
- That's impossible.

1177
00:51:39,167 --> 00:51:41,600
- [Tom] You got a
lozenge or something?

1178
00:51:41,600 --> 00:51:43,833
- Would you have thought
possible what he's already done?

1179
00:51:43,833 --> 00:51:45,767
- He's worn plaid with stripes?

1180
00:51:45,767 --> 00:51:46,633
- You yourself.

1181
00:51:46,633 --> 00:51:48,033
- [Mike] Spock.

1182
00:51:48,033 --> 00:51:49,533
- He's brought you back.

1183
00:51:49,533 --> 00:51:50,367
You live.

1184
00:51:50,367 --> 00:51:52,267
- [Crow] You live, Joe.

1185
00:51:52,267 --> 00:51:54,467
- Only a few years ago.

1186
00:51:54,467 --> 00:51:56,600
- [Tom] Whoa, hey,
watch the table there.

1187
00:51:56,600 --> 00:51:58,333
Neck juice all over the floor.

1188
00:51:58,333 --> 00:52:00,500
- That's what he's
been doing up here

1189
00:52:00,500 --> 00:52:02,433
where no one would see his work.

1190
00:52:02,433 --> 00:52:03,667
- Yes.

1191
00:52:03,667 --> 00:52:05,367
- That and whoring
at the Moulin Rouge.

1192
00:52:05,367 --> 00:52:08,167
- Experimenting with
transplants on that.

1193
00:52:08,167 --> 00:52:09,000
And on me.

1194
00:52:10,967 --> 00:52:14,767
That he can tear away my
flesh time after time,

1195
00:52:14,767 --> 00:52:16,667
test after test.

1196
00:52:16,667 --> 00:52:18,400
- [Mike] But any job
has its downside.

1197
00:52:18,400 --> 00:52:20,833
- My hopes shattering
with each grafted arm

1198
00:52:20,833 --> 00:52:21,933
he fastened to me.

1199
00:52:23,133 --> 00:52:26,167
Watching it wither and warp.

1200
00:52:26,167 --> 00:52:28,267
- [Tom] Why he gave my hand
rich Corinthian leather

1201
00:52:28,267 --> 00:52:29,867
I'll never know.

1202
00:52:29,867 --> 00:52:32,833
- Look, you know they
say there's always
someone worse off?

1203
00:52:32,833 --> 00:52:34,067
I'm that person.

1204
00:52:34,067 --> 00:52:38,000
- You see, he's learned
from his mistakes.

1205
00:52:38,000 --> 00:52:39,133
- [Mike] Guys, I
think he likes her.

1206
00:52:39,133 --> 00:52:40,667
I think he's gonna ask her out.

1207
00:52:40,667 --> 00:52:42,300
- [Tom] Ooh!

1208
00:52:42,300 --> 00:52:46,033
- And you stayed with
him, helping him in
his grotesque work

1209
00:52:46,033 --> 00:52:47,833
that he claims is for science.

1210
00:52:47,833 --> 00:52:50,067
- Hey, you were gonna
marry him, okay?

1211
00:52:50,067 --> 00:52:51,600
- There's no place
for me on the outside.

1212
00:52:51,600 --> 00:52:56,567
This, a world where eyes
would look upon me with pity

1213
00:52:57,767 --> 00:53:01,133
and people would turn
away from me in disgust.

1214
00:53:01,133 --> 00:53:02,900
- [Mike] And then I'd show
them my hand. Thank you!

1215
00:53:02,900 --> 00:53:04,200
It's a one-arm joke.

1216
00:53:05,433 --> 00:53:07,000
- The alcoholic has his bottle.

1217
00:53:07,000 --> 00:53:08,567
- [Tom] Uh, yeah, right he does.

1218
00:53:08,567 --> 00:53:10,400
- The dope addict his needle.

1219
00:53:10,400 --> 00:53:13,333
- The chocoholic his Godivas.

1220
00:53:13,333 --> 00:53:14,800
- I had my research.

1221
00:53:14,800 --> 00:53:17,033
- [Mike] And I had my body.
Could you change my neck juice?

1222
00:53:17,033 --> 00:53:19,533
- To be a surgeon,
it was my life.

1223
00:53:21,667 --> 00:53:25,967
Then one night in
the laboratory, there
was an accident.

1224
00:53:25,967 --> 00:53:27,567
- [Tom] I wet 'em.

1225
00:53:32,100 --> 00:53:33,500
- I have a power.

1226
00:53:34,633 --> 00:53:36,033
This liquid that
he's pumped into me.

1227
00:53:36,033 --> 00:53:37,400
- [Mike] Does it
have NutraSweet?

1228
00:53:37,400 --> 00:53:38,800
- My brain burns with it.

1229
00:53:38,800 --> 00:53:41,100
- Paul Newman's
Sockarooni sauce.

1230
00:53:41,100 --> 00:53:43,500
- That thing inside
and I are in touch.

1231
00:53:43,500 --> 00:53:45,533
Want me to prove it?

1232
00:53:45,533 --> 00:53:47,100
- You can prove nothing.

1233
00:53:48,133 --> 00:53:49,367
You're powerless.

1234
00:53:50,767 --> 00:53:53,633
- I'll show you
how powerless I am.

1235
00:53:53,633 --> 00:53:55,100
- [Tom] Alakazam, huzzah!

1236
00:53:55,100 --> 00:53:55,933
Oh, well.

1237
00:53:57,100 --> 00:53:57,900
- You.

1238
00:53:59,133 --> 00:54:00,333
Behind that door.

1239
00:54:00,333 --> 00:54:01,400
- Marilyn Chambers?

1240
00:54:01,400 --> 00:54:02,467
(something knocking)

1241
00:54:02,467 --> 00:54:03,700
- [Tom] Master locks.

1242
